#: ../../source/reference/design/index.md:37
msgid "The whole algorithm at a glance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/index.md:39
msgid ""
"Documents are classified per document, the union is scheduled into steps,"
" each step runs page classes through pipeline bundles, and the results "
"resolve against the promise map before the tables are written"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/index.md:43
msgid ""
"**One run, end to end.** Each document is opened and classified **on its "
"own**, so that a format's page-class finalizer sees one document's pages."
" The classified pages of every document are then poured into **one** "
"schedule, which processes them in steps; a step's results become the next"
" step's filter. Every page of a class goes through that class's **bundle "
"of pipelines**, each three segments long, and what comes out is either an"
" entity or a promise. Entities resolve against the accumulated promise "
"map at the end, and the whole run writes **one** set of tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/design/index.md:51
msgid ""
"The two halves of that picture are the two halves of this section. "
"Everything up to the schedule is about *which pages get processed and in "
"what order*; everything after it is about *what a page becomes*."
msgstr ""

